# TabTidy — Privacy Policy

**Last updated: April 2026**

## Overview

TabTidy is a Chrome extension that groups your open tabs by domain. This policy explains how the extension handles data.

## Data collection

TabTidy does **not** collect, store, transmit or share any personal data or browsing data.

## How it works

- When you click **Group all tabs**, the extension reads the URLs and titles of your currently open tabs to determine their domain
- Tabs are grouped locally in your browser using Chrome's native Tab Groups API
- No data leaves your device
- No data is sent to any server
- No analytics or tracking of any kind is used
- Tab data is only accessed at the moment you click the button — the extension does not run in the background

## Permissions

| Permission | Reason |
|---|---|
| `tabs` | To read the URLs and titles of open tabs in order to group them by domain |
| `tabGroups` | To create, name, colour and collapse tab groups in Chrome |

